1
00:00:06,141 --> 00:00:07,735
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:09,320
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:22,251 --> 00:00:25,372
- Thank you for the food.
- Sure, enjoy.

4
00:00:42,727 --> 00:00:45,977
Kimchi fried rice is your comfort food?

5
00:00:46,031 --> 00:00:49,639
Yes. When I eat kimchi fried rice,

6
00:00:50,897 --> 00:00:53,579
all that weariness just disappears.

7
00:00:53,971 --> 00:00:56,371
The sadness melts away like snow.

8
00:00:56,504 --> 00:00:58,251
Isn't that amazing?

9
00:01:00,037 --> 00:01:04,631
A little jealous here, but okay. Noted.

10
00:01:07,398 --> 00:01:09,078
This is so good.

11
00:01:09,285 --> 00:01:11,175
How are you this good at cooking?

12
00:01:11,725 --> 00:01:16,977
Of all the kimchi fried rice I've had,
this is the top of the top. The best.

13
00:01:17,170 --> 00:01:18,584
The best.

14
00:01:19,481 --> 00:01:23,623
I'll make you kimchi fried rice every day.

15
00:01:24,824 --> 00:01:26,913
How did I get this lucky, Han Gyu Rim?

16
00:01:27,931 --> 00:01:29,630
Am I allowed to be this happy?

17
00:01:29,684 --> 00:01:32,658
You're happy? So am I.

18
00:01:34,890 --> 00:01:36,124
This is so good.

19
00:01:39,085 --> 00:01:41,894
We don't usually make anything
off the menu,

20
00:01:42,301 --> 00:01:44,608
but I'm making an exception for you.

21
00:01:49,356 --> 00:01:50,941
Thank you.

22
00:01:51,077 --> 00:01:53,757
Please enjoy.

23
00:02:34,071 --> 00:02:35,915
This is completely burned.

24
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:54,504
Chef.

25
00:03:59,711 --> 00:04:03,003
The whole staff is walking on eggshells
around you right now.

26
00:04:06,738 --> 00:04:10,707
- Drink some ice water and snap out of it.
- Sure.

27
00:04:13,677 --> 00:04:14,951
What was I doing just now?

28
00:04:14,976 --> 00:04:17,271
You were burning the salmon, Chef.

29
00:04:30,318 --> 00:04:33,755
From now on, no off-menu dishes. Not ever.

30
00:04:39,265 --> 00:04:42,054
Thank you for the meal.

31
00:04:56,564 --> 00:04:57,633
Gyu Rim.

32
00:05:02,964 --> 00:05:05,587
Please don't come to our restaurant again.

33
00:05:06,833 --> 00:05:09,092
- Why not?
- You know why.

34
00:05:11,556 --> 00:05:12,618
Know what?

35
00:05:12,904 --> 00:05:15,332
Why are you like this?
That's not like you.

36
00:05:18,532 --> 00:05:21,565
All right. I won't come back.

37
00:05:22,885 --> 00:05:24,832
I wasn't reading the room.

38
00:05:25,537 --> 00:05:26,956
This is how I'm supposed to be, right?

39
00:05:27,845 --> 00:05:30,055
The Han Gyu Rim you knew.

40
00:05:30,645 --> 00:05:31,851
Exactly.

41
00:05:33,170 --> 00:05:34,886
That's the kind of person you were.

42
00:05:34,911 --> 00:05:37,405
You were never the type to show up
out of nowhere, corner someone,

43
00:05:37,429 --> 00:05:41,644
stir everything up and leave them a wreck.

44
00:05:43,465 --> 00:05:44,983
Why can't I be?

45
00:05:47,197 --> 00:05:48,234
Sorry?

46
00:05:48,791 --> 00:05:54,550
Cornering people, stirring things up,
leaving them a wreck,

47
00:05:55,397 --> 00:05:57,831
everyone else seems to manage it fine...

48
00:05:59,004 --> 00:06:02,524
So why can't I?

49
00:06:03,925 --> 00:06:05,141
Well, that's...

50
00:06:07,104 --> 00:06:08,987
Why are you doing this all of a sudden?

51
00:06:09,565 --> 00:06:14,048
You're the last person
I ever expected this from.

52
00:06:16,465 --> 00:06:21,486
Just once, I want to stop caring
what everyone else thinks,

53
00:06:22,622 --> 00:06:24,450
and just be selfish.

54
00:06:25,277 --> 00:06:29,911
Forget what I've done to people,
who I've hurt,

55
00:06:31,118 --> 00:06:36,215
forget all my mistakes
and just be shameless about it...

56
00:06:38,365 --> 00:06:40,302
Am I not allowed to live like that?

57
00:06:42,365 --> 00:06:47,014
Just stop putting up with things,
stop being so considerate,

58
00:06:47,875 --> 00:06:49,995
and just follow my heart...

59
00:06:52,345 --> 00:06:53,754
Am I not allowed...

60
00:06:55,408 --> 00:06:56,961
to live like that?

61
00:07:21,424 --> 00:07:24,728
Of course you are. Absolutely.

62
00:07:25,904 --> 00:07:28,456
It's a free country. Why wouldn't you be?

63
00:07:29,337 --> 00:07:30,790
You're only human.

64
00:07:52,325 --> 00:07:55,075
You must have missed her badly.
You held out well.

65
00:07:55,551 --> 00:07:58,431
I was on edge, thinking
you'd insist on serving her yourself.

66
00:07:59,351 --> 00:08:00,526
Got a cigarette?

67
00:08:00,763 --> 00:08:02,023
What's with the cigarette?

68
00:08:02,048 --> 00:08:03,925
You quit when you started cooking.

69
00:08:04,731 --> 00:08:06,145
I said, do you have one?

70
00:08:08,178 --> 00:08:10,725
No. I'm out. I have to go buy some myself.

71
00:08:12,453 --> 00:08:14,149
Anybody around here got cigarettes?

72
00:08:15,925 --> 00:08:17,393
You were completely thrown, weren't you?

73
00:08:17,951 --> 00:08:19,849
I was totally freaking out.

74
00:08:20,052 --> 00:08:23,106
I never dreamed Gyu Rim
would show up at our place.

75
00:08:23,131 --> 00:08:25,050
I'm going out for cigarettes.

76
00:08:25,578 --> 00:08:28,029
If it's this hard,
just end it with Seo Hyeon.

77
00:08:28,064 --> 00:08:29,700
End it with her and go to Han Gyu Rim.

78
00:08:29,725 --> 00:08:33,430
Gyu Rim looks pretty messed up too.
She's still not over you.

79
00:08:33,645 --> 00:08:36,300
I just want a smoke. Why the nonsense?

80
00:08:36,325 --> 00:08:37,885
You want to go to her. You know you do.

81
00:08:41,331 --> 00:08:43,783
You don't have a shred
of feeling for Seo Hyeon.

82
00:08:44,770 --> 00:08:47,205
I know you want to keep your word
to Seo Hyeon,

83
00:08:47,230 --> 00:08:48,999
but so what if you break it?

84
00:08:50,098 --> 00:08:52,573
Her mother is dead set against it anyway,

85
00:08:52,839 --> 00:08:55,043
and not everyone lives up
to their word the way you do.

86
00:08:55,068 --> 00:08:57,985
Hey. How many of these do you smoke a day?

87
00:08:58,298 --> 00:09:00,520
It was almost full this morning.
You went through the whole pack?

88
00:09:00,544 --> 00:09:03,157
It wrecks your brain cells and your bones.

89
00:09:03,182 --> 00:09:04,814
Are you trying to die young?

90
00:09:05,048 --> 00:09:08,701
With that attitude, what's the point
of working out or taking vitamins?

91
00:09:09,205 --> 00:09:11,060
You absolute idiot.

92
00:09:12,758 --> 00:09:16,353
Hey. From this second on,
you're done with cigarettes.

93
00:09:16,625 --> 00:09:19,895
A restaurant owner chain-smoking?
What a terrible image.

94
00:09:20,071 --> 00:09:21,480
Just try not quitting.

95
00:09:21,505 --> 00:09:23,697
You're fired tomorrow. Understood?

96
00:09:31,751 --> 00:09:34,241
Sure. Take it out on me.

97
00:09:34,970 --> 00:09:37,400
Yelling at me is the only thing
that'll settle you down.

98
00:09:38,969 --> 00:09:40,302
Why me?

99
00:09:40,675 --> 00:09:45,079
Why do I get nothing
but lunatics around me,

100
00:09:45,656 --> 00:09:48,077
putting me through all this?

101
00:09:51,438 --> 00:09:53,276
If he says quit, I quit.

102
00:10:25,665 --> 00:10:27,592
I missed you...

103
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:33,427
You could have at least shown your face.

104
00:10:36,405 --> 00:10:37,740
So you're saying...

105
00:10:40,351 --> 00:10:42,220
never come back.

106
00:11:03,639 --> 00:11:05,151
Don't come back, Han Gyu Rim.

107
00:11:07,247 --> 00:11:08,915
I won't make it for you again.

108
00:11:12,728 --> 00:11:14,468
What you're saying,

109
00:11:16,313 --> 00:11:17,757
I understand completely.

110
00:11:20,155 --> 00:11:21,615
Even so...

111
00:11:26,407 --> 00:11:28,112
the kimchi fried rice...

112
00:11:33,903 --> 00:11:35,782
was so good.

113
00:11:39,271 --> 00:11:40,396
For everything...

114
00:11:42,663 --> 00:11:44,252
thank you...

115
00:11:47,142 --> 00:11:48,745
so much.

116
00:12:08,773 --> 00:12:10,525
Gyu Rim went to Mu Jin's restaurant?

117
00:12:10,605 --> 00:12:14,147
Yes. She ordered kimchi fried rice,
which isn't even on the menu,

118
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:16,020
and Mu Jin made it for her.

119
00:12:16,684 --> 00:12:18,689
Does she still like him,
after all this time?

120
00:12:19,698 --> 00:12:20,952
You didn't know?

121
00:12:22,564 --> 00:12:25,366
And how does he feel about her?

122
00:12:26,224 --> 00:12:29,003
The staff say he's seeing someone.

123
00:12:30,345 --> 00:12:32,360
Just because there's a goalie
doesn't mean you can't score.

124
00:12:33,016 --> 00:12:36,953
I don't know about the goalie,
but the goalpost looked pretty solid.

125
00:12:37,116 --> 00:12:40,295
Her saves are insane, and there's
no gap to get the ball through.

126
00:12:40,356 --> 00:12:43,246
If she liked him that much,
why did she break up with him?

127
00:12:43,891 --> 00:12:46,978
Hey. Why do you think?

128
00:12:47,278 --> 00:12:49,447
You, me,

129
00:12:49,681 --> 00:12:51,335
Dad, Han Gyu Yeong, Han Gyu O.

130
00:12:51,837 --> 00:12:54,600
This miserable family of ours.

131
00:12:54,638 --> 00:12:56,813
She didn't want to drag him down with us.

132
00:12:56,838 --> 00:12:59,533
Seriously? It was because of us?

133
00:13:01,164 --> 00:13:04,329
Some things you're scary smart about,

134
00:13:04,354 --> 00:13:07,422
and some things you're hopeless at. Right?

135
00:13:07,731 --> 00:13:09,679
Cheap little brats.

136
00:13:09,942 --> 00:13:13,949
If you're washing anyway,
could you hang mine out too?

137
00:13:15,871 --> 00:13:18,537
You picked out only mine and left it.

138
00:13:19,356 --> 00:13:22,920
We were running a load anyway,
so we threw it in to save water.

139
00:13:22,945 --> 00:13:25,340
You hang your own, Dad.

140
00:13:25,431 --> 00:13:28,159
If you're going to live with Gyu O,
start practicing now.

141
00:13:28,184 --> 00:13:30,421
Here, shake it out. See? Shake it.

142
00:13:30,657 --> 00:13:32,272
I'm not living with Gyu O.

143
00:13:32,624 --> 00:13:34,364
I'm living with Gyu Rim, Gyeol,
and you two.

144
00:13:34,502 --> 00:13:35,737
Says who?

145
00:13:35,825 --> 00:13:39,068
If you abandon me,
the whole neighborhood will hear about it.

146
00:13:39,093 --> 00:13:41,601
That you're
the most ungrateful kids alive.

147
00:13:41,684 --> 00:13:44,384
With a rumor like that,
how will you show your faces at school?

148
00:13:45,537 --> 00:13:48,334
So let's live together. All right?

149
00:13:48,891 --> 00:13:51,534
And you two help me convince Gyu Rim.

150
00:13:52,018 --> 00:13:55,257
If I die like this,
you'll regret it the rest of your lives.

151
00:13:55,282 --> 00:13:57,311
You're the one who abandoned us first.

152
00:13:58,705 --> 00:14:00,297
Me? When?

153
00:14:00,445 --> 00:14:03,480
If I had abandoned you,
would you have turned out this well?

154
00:14:03,505 --> 00:14:06,754
Gyu Rim raised us, not you.

155
00:14:07,305 --> 00:14:08,780
I raised you too.

156
00:14:08,905 --> 00:14:12,388
I changed your dirty diapers.
I pushed you in the walker.

157
00:14:12,685 --> 00:14:14,871
Either way, I'm the one who had you.

158
00:14:14,896 --> 00:14:16,397
Why did you have us at all?

159
00:14:17,084 --> 00:14:19,318
You never asked us if we wanted this.

160
00:14:19,951 --> 00:14:21,318
You little...

161
00:14:21,985 --> 00:14:25,245
You're asking me why I had you?

162
00:14:25,555 --> 00:14:27,491
I had you out of love. So what?

163
00:14:27,516 --> 00:14:31,108
I loved your mother so much
that we had you. Deal with it.

164
00:14:31,138 --> 00:14:34,807
Why does a married man with kids
go fall in love with another woman?

165
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:36,487
That's what I'm asking!

166
00:14:36,512 --> 00:14:38,880
Your mother is the one who seduced me.

167
00:14:38,905 --> 00:14:42,281
How do you not fall for a woman
even if it's all a trap?

168
00:14:42,306 --> 00:14:44,346
A man this full of love?

169
00:14:44,371 --> 00:14:48,056
If we'd never been born, you and Gyu Rim's
mother wouldn't have divorced.

170
00:14:48,085 --> 00:14:49,552
If we'd never been born,

171
00:14:49,678 --> 00:14:52,052
Gyu Rim wouldn't be struggling like this.

172
00:14:53,284 --> 00:14:55,571
Why? Did she say something?

173
00:14:56,685 --> 00:14:59,366
Did she blame you two
for making her life hard?

174
00:14:59,778 --> 00:15:03,034
Hey, Gyu Rim's been acting strange lately.

175
00:15:04,378 --> 00:15:09,633
Have you heard anything about her
joining some kind of cult?

176
00:15:13,058 --> 00:15:14,179
You little...

177
00:15:15,531 --> 00:15:20,233
If she ever picks on you
or makes you feel small, tell me.

178
00:15:20,458 --> 00:15:23,000
If she turns on you too,
the three of us will live on our own.

179
00:15:25,765 --> 00:15:27,205
When are you going to grow up, Dad?

180
00:15:27,471 --> 00:15:29,796
Around the day after tomorrow?

181
00:15:29,957 --> 00:15:32,067
Like that'll happen.

182
00:15:32,411 --> 00:15:37,376
I'll give everything I own to whoever
grows up first, you or Gyu Yeong.

183
00:15:37,687 --> 00:15:40,233
- How much do you even own?
- Never mind. Go hang all this.

184
00:15:40,824 --> 00:15:43,265
How much? Hey.

185
00:15:45,838 --> 00:15:47,382
These clueless kids.

186
00:15:56,528 --> 00:16:03,227
(Lottery Shop)

187
00:16:03,857 --> 00:16:07,498
Hello. Ten two-dollar
scratch tickets, please.

188
00:16:14,658 --> 00:16:15,658
Please.

189
00:16:16,637 --> 00:16:17,643
Nothing.

190
00:16:22,937 --> 00:16:25,961
It's a bust. Obviously a bust.

191
00:16:27,445 --> 00:16:30,316
With an attitude like that, you'd win?

192
00:16:32,291 --> 00:16:33,832
I'm asking you nicely.

193
00:16:33,862 --> 00:16:35,860
Could you just pretend you didn't see me
and keep walking?

194
00:16:35,898 --> 00:16:37,521
I meant to,

195
00:16:37,688 --> 00:16:40,133
but the second I see you, I feel this urge
to make something of you.

196
00:16:40,158 --> 00:16:41,831
Some sense of responsibility.

197
00:16:42,136 --> 00:16:43,291
You're the worst.

198
00:16:43,478 --> 00:16:45,611
The worst person I know.

199
00:16:45,651 --> 00:16:46,651
That so?

200
00:16:47,416 --> 00:16:50,398
You're the worst person I know too.

201
00:16:50,451 --> 00:16:53,707
That's the one thing
we agree on, isn't it?

202
00:17:01,664 --> 00:17:03,067
When is she ever going to shape up?

203
00:17:23,904 --> 00:17:25,299
What are you looking at?

204
00:17:27,164 --> 00:17:28,611
That's Seong Uk, isn't it?

205
00:17:29,962 --> 00:17:31,111
No, it's not.

206
00:17:31,136 --> 00:17:34,265
Has he lost his mind,
this close to the wedding?

207
00:17:36,250 --> 00:17:38,840
- What are you going to do?
- Go find him and beat him senseless.

208
00:17:38,865 --> 00:17:40,085
Why would you?

209
00:17:40,087 --> 00:17:42,265
He's earned a beating, hasn't he?

210
00:17:42,266 --> 00:17:43,791
Who are you to do anything?

211
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:48,765
I had you completely wrong.

212
00:17:48,919 --> 00:17:52,058
Call off the wedding. Call off everything!

213
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:53,991
It's none of your business.

214
00:17:53,993 --> 00:17:55,266
It is my business.

215
00:17:55,268 --> 00:17:57,105
Han Gyu Rim is like family to me,

216
00:17:58,171 --> 00:18:00,984
and you're her sister. Good enough?

217
00:18:01,611 --> 00:18:03,104
Just try saying one word about it.

218
00:18:03,129 --> 00:18:04,789
You're dead and so am I.

219
00:18:04,791 --> 00:18:07,362
So I just let a punk like that walk free?

220
00:18:07,364 --> 00:18:09,338
Yes. Just leave it alone!

221
00:18:09,911 --> 00:18:12,102
It's not a marriage for love anyway.

222
00:18:13,731 --> 00:18:18,044
Do you hear yourself right now?

223
00:18:20,324 --> 00:18:22,267
No matter what, I'm going through with it.

224
00:18:22,891 --> 00:18:25,009
Whatever that jerk does,

225
00:18:25,850 --> 00:18:27,004
I am getting married.

226
00:18:28,351 --> 00:18:30,741
Get in my way and I swear I'll kill you.

227
00:18:45,504 --> 00:18:46,764
Now what do we do?

228
00:18:46,945 --> 00:18:48,711
By complete accident,

229
00:18:48,713 --> 00:18:51,298
I knocked over the bucket of loaches.

230
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:53,744
My back isn't in great shape,

231
00:18:53,892 --> 00:18:55,970
so you'll have to pick them all up.

232
00:18:57,058 --> 00:18:59,438
- Me?
- Who else is here?

233
00:18:59,978 --> 00:19:02,204
Hurry up before customers come in.

234
00:19:05,045 --> 00:19:07,525
What? You can't do it?

235
00:19:08,151 --> 00:19:11,480
If it burns you up, write your notice
and go.

236
00:19:12,785 --> 00:19:14,904
No. I'll pick them all up.

237
00:19:24,502 --> 00:19:25,965
I hear you woke up.

238
00:19:26,125 --> 00:19:29,708
No more forcing yourself
to do what you hate?

239
00:19:29,891 --> 00:19:32,656
Thinking of yourself
instead of everyone else?

240
00:19:33,137 --> 00:19:36,406
I figured that's why
you turned down my Heung Sik.

241
00:19:36,807 --> 00:19:38,795
So why are you putting up with this now?

242
00:19:39,505 --> 00:19:40,978
Something this unfair,

243
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:43,198
and you're putting up with it in silence?

244
00:19:45,510 --> 00:19:48,837
Are you saving it all up to report
me as an abusive employer?

245
00:19:52,118 --> 00:19:53,859
Cat got your tongue?

246
00:19:55,538 --> 00:19:57,616
Because it doesn't feel unfair to me.

247
00:19:58,438 --> 00:19:59,438
What?

248
00:19:59,689 --> 00:20:01,390
What you ask of me,

249
00:20:01,892 --> 00:20:04,444
for some reason it never feels unfair.

250
00:20:06,470 --> 00:20:08,101
It wasn't an accident.

251
00:20:08,504 --> 00:20:12,222
I know live loaches
are the thing you're most afraid of,

252
00:20:12,372 --> 00:20:15,489
so I dumped them on purpose
to mess with you.

253
00:20:15,570 --> 00:20:16,944
Sucks, doesn't it?

254
00:20:22,818 --> 00:20:24,078
You stubborn thing.

255
00:20:24,388 --> 00:20:26,913
Fine. Let's see how unfair I can get,

256
00:20:27,327 --> 00:20:32,117
and how long you can hold out!

257
00:20:53,731 --> 00:20:55,369
Honey, are you all right?

258
00:20:58,118 --> 00:20:59,118
Sorry?

259
00:21:02,171 --> 00:21:05,608
Why are you looking
at me like that? Is my...

260
00:21:06,057 --> 00:21:07,615
Your mouth...

261
00:21:08,084 --> 00:21:09,521
Is there something on my face?

262
00:21:11,238 --> 00:21:13,051
What's wrong with my face?

263
00:21:16,158 --> 00:21:17,483
I've lost my mind.

264
00:21:17,811 --> 00:21:19,153
It's all right.

265
00:21:45,231 --> 00:21:46,231
Honey.

266
00:21:48,751 --> 00:21:49,854
Are you all right?

267
00:21:50,231 --> 00:21:51,277
Have some tea.

268
00:21:52,938 --> 00:21:53,938
I'm sorry.

269
00:21:54,651 --> 00:21:57,031
- I must have scared you.
- Not at all.

270
00:21:59,851 --> 00:22:02,008
I was so deep in my thoughts,

271
00:22:03,290 --> 00:22:05,530
I didn't even know what I was doing.

272
00:22:08,078 --> 00:22:09,724
Then what were you thinking about?

273
00:22:09,852 --> 00:22:11,211
Can I know too?

274
00:22:15,483 --> 00:22:18,158
Do I have to wait
until you want to tell me?

275
00:22:23,565 --> 00:22:24,631
It's all right if you don't.

276
00:22:25,224 --> 00:22:26,378
I'll be going.

277
00:22:27,305 --> 00:22:28,358
I'll tell you.

278
00:22:32,738 --> 00:22:34,744
I'll tell you everything.

279
00:22:37,137 --> 00:22:38,137
What is it?

280
00:22:43,998 --> 00:22:45,245
That girl,

281
00:22:47,595 --> 00:22:48,768
she's my daughter.

282
00:22:51,771 --> 00:22:53,991
The one Mu Jin was seeing,

283
00:22:56,778 --> 00:22:58,492
that's Gyu Rim.

284
00:23:07,250 --> 00:23:08,539
That's why...

285
00:23:10,935 --> 00:23:13,371
That's why I fought it so hard.

286
00:23:16,751 --> 00:23:18,465
I'm sorry, honey.

287
00:23:19,229 --> 00:23:21,544
To you, and to Seo Hyeon.

288
00:23:23,245 --> 00:23:24,811
I'm so sorry.

289
00:23:40,918 --> 00:23:42,290
Mom.

290
00:23:48,337 --> 00:23:49,337
Mom.

291
00:23:49,827 --> 00:23:51,111
Yes, Seo Hyeon.

292
00:23:56,971 --> 00:23:58,531
Mom, have you been crying?

293
00:23:59,022 --> 00:24:02,770
No. It's just my allergies.

294
00:24:02,965 --> 00:24:04,547
Did you make her cry?

295
00:24:10,504 --> 00:24:12,733
Mom, can I talk to you for a...

296
00:24:13,586 --> 00:24:16,078
Never mind. Dad, you should hear this too.

297
00:24:33,564 --> 00:24:35,038
Something did feel off.

298
00:24:35,698 --> 00:24:37,554
You're not usually like this,

299
00:24:37,668 --> 00:24:40,729
and watching you tear into Mu Jin
and shut him down for no reason,

300
00:24:40,877 --> 00:24:43,338
I had a nagging feeling
something was there.

301
00:24:44,991 --> 00:24:48,111
I'm not good at going around things,
so I'll ask you straight.

302
00:24:50,871 --> 00:24:53,144
Is Mu Jin your son?

303
00:24:56,184 --> 00:24:57,403
Seo Hyeon.

304
00:24:57,778 --> 00:24:59,238
If he isn't, just say he isn't.

305
00:24:59,804 --> 00:25:01,864
Is Mu Jin your son?

306
00:25:03,271 --> 00:25:04,511
What are you talking about?

307
00:25:05,069 --> 00:25:07,057
Where would you get such a ridiculous...

308
00:25:07,185 --> 00:25:10,371
When I think about him and Mu Jin,
there's too much that lines up.

309
00:25:11,098 --> 00:25:12,200
The same blood type,

310
00:25:12,275 --> 00:25:14,204
their coffee and wine tastes match up
in ways that make no sense,

311
00:25:14,305 --> 00:25:15,652
they're both Erik Satie fanatics,

312
00:25:16,133 --> 00:25:18,405
they both get hit by pollen allergies,

313
00:25:18,407 --> 00:25:20,059
they both live with colds all winter,

314
00:25:20,061 --> 00:25:22,131
they both like soft rice
and dipping instead of pouring...

315
00:25:22,133 --> 00:25:24,026
You're overstepping now.

316
00:25:24,457 --> 00:25:26,194
How could you say
that about your father...

317
00:25:26,454 --> 00:25:29,385
Don't you know what kind of man he is?

318
00:25:29,891 --> 00:25:31,324
How could you say such a thing?

319
00:25:32,004 --> 00:25:33,444
Explain yourself, Dad.

320
00:25:34,198 --> 00:25:35,431
Am I overreacting?

321
00:25:35,771 --> 00:25:38,491
Am I making a terrible mistake
right now, Dad?

322
00:25:39,962 --> 00:25:43,124
Seo Hyeon, it's nothing like that.

323
00:25:44,921 --> 00:25:47,973
I fought so hard against you and Mu Jin,

324
00:25:47,974 --> 00:25:50,137
and it's made you oversensitive.

325
00:25:51,625 --> 00:25:52,984
I'll tell you everything.

326
00:25:53,971 --> 00:25:56,126
- I'll tell you all of it.
- It's true.

327
00:26:01,305 --> 00:26:04,364
It's true. Mu Jin is my son.

328
00:26:04,597 --> 00:26:05,597
Honey.

329
00:26:08,785 --> 00:26:09,799
He's my son,

330
00:26:10,633 --> 00:26:11,659
but for various reasons,

331
00:26:12,180 --> 00:26:15,565
Chairwoman Hong has been raising him.

332
00:26:18,178 --> 00:26:20,777
Seo Hyeon, no. It's nothing like that.

333
00:26:22,451 --> 00:26:24,489
I was just so frustrated,

334
00:26:24,607 --> 00:26:26,463
I threw out the first thing
that came to me,

335
00:26:27,110 --> 00:26:30,414
and you don't get to take it
that seriously, Dad.

336
00:26:31,324 --> 00:26:33,540
You're supposed to shout,
"What do you take me for?"

337
00:26:33,783 --> 00:26:35,624
You're supposed to scold me.
That's normal.

338
00:26:36,451 --> 00:26:37,549
No, listen.

339
00:26:38,123 --> 00:26:41,195
I had him before I was married,
when I was young and stupid,

340
00:26:42,343 --> 00:26:46,258
and Chairwoman Hong has been
raising him ever since,

341
00:26:46,724 --> 00:26:48,764
and I only found out myself recently.

342
00:26:48,811 --> 00:26:49,811
Honey.

343
00:26:50,523 --> 00:26:52,127
No, Seo Hyeon, it's not like that.

344
00:26:52,129 --> 00:26:53,522
- I'm sorry, honey.
- It's not like that.

345
00:26:53,524 --> 00:26:54,864
I'm sorry I couldn't tell you.

346
00:26:54,866 --> 00:26:56,851
Seo Hyeon, I'll tell you everything.

347
00:26:56,876 --> 00:26:59,993
Seo Hyeon, let me tell you everything.

348
00:27:00,331 --> 00:27:02,028
What is this, seriously?

349
00:27:03,818 --> 00:27:06,022
I'm too scared to make a joke now.

350
00:27:06,410 --> 00:27:07,864
I can't even joke around.

351
00:27:08,217 --> 00:27:10,300
What is this, seriously?

352
00:27:11,620 --> 00:27:13,381
Seo Hyeon.

353
00:27:13,406 --> 00:27:15,650
- Honey.
- Honey!

354
00:27:17,271 --> 00:27:19,598
Why would you tell a lie like that?

355
00:27:21,770 --> 00:27:22,922
Let's go with it.

356
00:27:23,845 --> 00:27:25,758
Let's say Mu Jin is my son.

357
00:27:26,027 --> 00:27:30,070
So Seo Hyeon and Mu Jin can't happen.

358
00:27:30,751 --> 00:27:32,862
They can't be together anyway, can they?

359
00:27:32,984 --> 00:27:35,129
So whatever the reason,
what's the problem?

360
00:27:35,631 --> 00:27:37,254
It's because of me.

361
00:27:37,449 --> 00:27:40,118
All you had to do was tell her the truth,

362
00:27:40,258 --> 00:27:43,080
so why are you taking all
of it on yourself?

363
00:27:44,602 --> 00:27:47,714
No. I'm going
to tell Seo Hyeon everything.

364
00:27:47,817 --> 00:27:51,858
If you tell her the truth,
she'll never look at you again.

365
00:27:54,205 --> 00:27:55,451
Are you all right with that?

366
00:27:55,898 --> 00:27:56,944
I'm not.

367
00:27:58,404 --> 00:28:02,925
I don't want my daughter Seo Hyeon
to lose a mother all over again.

368
00:28:04,245 --> 00:28:06,099
Think how you raised that girl.

369
00:28:06,945 --> 00:28:08,766
Think how much she loves you.

370
00:28:09,058 --> 00:28:10,678
She loves you more than me.

371
00:28:11,918 --> 00:28:13,244
Even so,

372
00:28:14,978 --> 00:28:16,504
does this make any sense?

373
00:28:17,511 --> 00:28:20,478
Mu Jin being your son? How does that work?

374
00:28:20,480 --> 00:28:21,480
It doesn't.

375
00:28:21,798 --> 00:28:24,071
It has to make no sense
for her to back off.

376
00:28:24,511 --> 00:28:26,131
You know how Seo Hyeon is.

377
00:28:26,438 --> 00:28:29,404
She only gives up when something
makes no sense to her.

378
00:28:29,406 --> 00:28:30,406
Honey.

379
00:28:31,064 --> 00:28:32,064
I know. I do.

380
00:28:32,675 --> 00:28:34,471
I know how absurd this is,

381
00:28:35,099 --> 00:28:38,683
but I'll find a way to fix it,

382
00:28:39,144 --> 00:28:41,042
so just do as I say...

383
00:28:41,242 --> 00:28:44,208
and don't say a word.

384
00:28:47,307 --> 00:28:48,359
All right?

385
00:28:49,681 --> 00:28:50,826
It's all right.

386
00:28:54,711 --> 00:28:55,711
What?

387
00:28:58,405 --> 00:28:59,625
Say that again.

388
00:29:00,385 --> 00:29:02,391
Mu Jin is whose son now?

389
00:29:03,458 --> 00:29:04,487
Mine.

390
00:29:04,715 --> 00:29:06,636
So let's say he's my son.

391
00:29:06,777 --> 00:29:07,777
Just listen.

392
00:29:08,218 --> 00:29:11,160
Listen. Back when I was young and stupid,

393
00:29:11,162 --> 00:29:13,745
I got a girl pregnant before marriage.

394
00:29:14,055 --> 00:29:18,076
And you wanted a son,
so you took him in and raised him.

395
00:29:18,698 --> 00:29:20,586
So I'm not even his real mother now?

396
00:29:21,598 --> 00:29:22,658
That's how it works out.

397
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:24,178
Hey.

398
00:29:24,849 --> 00:29:28,453
Why do we need this insane setup?

399
00:29:28,904 --> 00:29:29,904
"Why?"

400
00:29:31,930 --> 00:29:35,796
Because nothing less
will make Seo Hyeon leave Mu Jin.

401
00:29:36,142 --> 00:29:38,934
I told you I never have anything
to laugh about these days,

402
00:29:38,959 --> 00:29:40,783
so you came to make me laugh, is that it?

403
00:29:40,978 --> 00:29:44,224
It's funny, all right. Hilarious.

404
00:29:46,105 --> 00:29:47,725
You owe me.

405
00:29:47,932 --> 00:29:49,598
- What?
- Did you forget?

406
00:29:50,803 --> 00:29:53,593
Back in college,
on that rock climb with the mountain club,

407
00:29:53,841 --> 00:29:56,305
I saved you from falling off that cliff.

408
00:29:56,671 --> 00:29:58,318
What did you say to me then?

409
00:29:58,605 --> 00:30:02,078
That someday you'd get a chance
to save me,

410
00:30:02,103 --> 00:30:03,975
and when it came, you'd repay the debt.

411
00:30:04,418 --> 00:30:06,351
- You promised.
- Are you dying?

412
00:30:07,130 --> 00:30:09,610
So pay that debt now.

413
00:30:10,723 --> 00:30:13,258
I know it's outrageous and absurd,

414
00:30:13,597 --> 00:30:16,797
but at least keep our stories straight
for Seo Hyeon's sake.

415
00:30:16,822 --> 00:30:19,374
No matter how badly you want
to keep Mu Jin and Seo Hyeon apart,

416
00:30:19,409 --> 00:30:21,205
how do you come up
with something this insane?

417
00:30:21,207 --> 00:30:23,218
A grade schooler would laugh at you.

418
00:30:23,220 --> 00:30:26,592
Fine. Laugh at me, blame me,
I'll take all of it,

419
00:30:27,379 --> 00:30:29,471
but can't you just do me this one favor?

420
00:30:29,496 --> 00:30:31,934
- Forget it, you idiot.
- Hey.

421
00:30:32,785 --> 00:30:34,464
If you want to play crazy, do it alone.

422
00:30:34,466 --> 00:30:36,618
Why drag me into it?

423
00:30:36,678 --> 00:30:39,426
So I'm supposed to know
they're brother and sister...

424
00:30:39,427 --> 00:30:40,658
and marry them off anyway...

425
00:30:41,465 --> 00:30:42,465
Hey,

426
00:30:42,865 --> 00:30:44,249
I can't even get the words out.

427
00:30:44,251 --> 00:30:46,538
Have you actually lost your mind?

428
00:30:46,765 --> 00:30:49,389
Then what do I do?
Should I get on my knees again?

429
00:30:49,391 --> 00:30:51,863
- Should I kneel again?
- Kneel for what?

430
00:30:51,888 --> 00:30:56,176
If you help me this time,

431
00:30:56,178 --> 00:30:58,191
I'll count it as you saving my life twice,

432
00:30:58,192 --> 00:31:00,325
and I'll spend the rest
of my life repaying it.

433
00:31:00,471 --> 00:31:01,885
So please, just do this for me.

434
00:31:01,910 --> 00:31:04,159
All right, I'm sorry.

435
00:31:04,258 --> 00:31:06,395
I'm sorry you suddenly aren't
his birth mother,

436
00:31:06,397 --> 00:31:08,258
and I'm sorry for this whole situation...

437
00:31:08,439 --> 00:31:09,765
So please. Come on,

438
00:31:10,054 --> 00:31:12,413
Ok Seon. Chairwoman Hong.

439
00:31:13,414 --> 00:31:14,644
You think I'd ask if I had any other way?

440
00:31:17,604 --> 00:31:18,604
Seriously.

441
00:31:22,551 --> 00:31:24,207
You must have heard him wrong.

442
00:31:24,817 --> 00:31:25,931
Does that even make sense?

443
00:31:26,278 --> 00:31:28,291
I was just saying whatever came to mind...

444
00:31:30,545 --> 00:31:33,425
His jokes go too far.

445
00:31:35,185 --> 00:31:36,365
Check your phone.

446
00:31:36,591 --> 00:31:37,930
There'll be a message from him...

447
00:31:38,017 --> 00:31:39,325
saying he was only joking.

448
00:31:40,105 --> 00:31:41,791
He messaged me a little while ago.

449
00:31:42,218 --> 00:31:45,144
Saying he doesn't know
how to make it up to me.

450
00:31:45,182 --> 00:31:46,182
That's...

451
00:31:48,792 --> 00:31:50,904
That's real? Seriously?

452
00:31:53,525 --> 00:31:54,944
I should have pretended not to know.

453
00:31:56,491 --> 00:31:58,951
I should never have asked.

454
00:32:04,175 --> 00:32:06,265
I don't believe it. I can't.

455
00:32:06,418 --> 00:32:08,200
How could he and Mu Jin's mother
do something so irresponsible,

456
00:32:08,202 --> 00:32:09,931
so shameless...

457
00:32:12,158 --> 00:32:14,620
It can't be. How does this make sense?

458
00:32:15,971 --> 00:32:17,831
I should have at least had a child
with Mu Jin.

459
00:32:17,925 --> 00:32:18,925
Hey,

460
00:32:19,087 --> 00:32:20,431
where do you get this soap-opera talk...

461
00:32:24,145 --> 00:32:25,305
How far did the two of you go?

462
00:32:25,678 --> 00:32:28,251
- Did you ever kiss?
- We'd have to meet first.

463
00:32:28,484 --> 00:32:31,344
My mom wouldn't even let us meet.

464
00:32:32,471 --> 00:32:34,151
And even then, my Mu Jin...

465
00:32:34,486 --> 00:32:38,024
can't so much as hold a hand
unless he loves the woman...

466
00:32:43,964 --> 00:32:45,158
Does Mu Jin know?

467
00:32:46,751 --> 00:32:48,458
Have you told him?

468
00:32:53,574 --> 00:32:55,297
Honestly.

469
00:32:57,925 --> 00:33:00,581
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

470
00:33:16,991 --> 00:33:17,991
Sir.

471
00:33:19,445 --> 00:33:22,115
Sit down.

472
00:33:24,271 --> 00:33:26,028
You've been drinking a lot lately.

473
00:33:26,393 --> 00:33:27,751
In the daytime, even.

474
00:33:31,337 --> 00:33:33,180
Has Seo Hyeon called you?

475
00:33:33,931 --> 00:33:36,738
No. Is something wrong?

476
00:33:38,650 --> 00:33:41,141
Your mother didn't call you either?

477
00:33:42,509 --> 00:33:43,837
What's this about, sir?

478
00:33:46,777 --> 00:33:49,458
- Want a drink?
- No, thank you.

479
00:33:51,697 --> 00:33:53,028
I'll have one glass.

480
00:33:53,858 --> 00:33:57,018
- Could we get another glass?
- Yes, of course.

481
00:33:59,145 --> 00:34:00,151
Mu Jin.

482
00:34:03,244 --> 00:34:05,518
That woman you were seeing,

483
00:34:07,457 --> 00:34:10,770
is she Han Gyu Rim?

484
00:34:16,611 --> 00:34:17,821
So it is.

485
00:34:18,661 --> 00:34:20,677
It is Han Gyu Rim, isn't it?

486
00:34:34,037 --> 00:34:36,364
Why bring up Gyu Rim all of a sudden...

487
00:34:37,690 --> 00:34:39,538
Han Gyu Rim...

488
00:34:40,606 --> 00:34:44,769
is the eldest daughter
Yun Hui left behind when she divorced.

489
00:34:45,584 --> 00:34:46,591
Sorry?

490
00:34:49,283 --> 00:34:50,424
Sir.

491
00:34:51,392 --> 00:34:55,290
That's why she fought so hard
against you and Seo Hyeon.

492
00:34:59,837 --> 00:35:01,484
Seo Hyeon still doesn't know.

493
00:35:03,051 --> 00:35:04,966
And I'm going to keep it that way.

494
00:35:05,818 --> 00:35:06,849
So,

495
00:35:09,398 --> 00:35:13,131
let's end it here, you and Seo Hyeon.

496
00:35:27,722 --> 00:35:31,204
I made up a reason for Seo Hyeon,
why she can't be with you,

497
00:35:31,228 --> 00:35:33,031
and it's a ridiculous one.

498
00:35:35,085 --> 00:35:36,785
Nothing less would make her give up.

499
00:35:39,758 --> 00:35:41,784
So I told her that you...

500
00:35:43,224 --> 00:35:45,708
Never mind. It's too absurd to repeat,

501
00:35:46,157 --> 00:35:50,656
so whatever Seo Hyeon says to you,
just say nothing back,

502
00:35:51,422 --> 00:35:55,754
and pull away from her.

503
00:35:56,891 --> 00:35:57,984
All right?

504
00:36:01,618 --> 00:36:02,684
My head is spinning.

505
00:36:05,204 --> 00:36:07,008
I'm sorry for putting you through this.

506
00:36:12,805 --> 00:36:18,885
Han Gyu Rim is the eldest daughter
Yun Hui left behind when she divorced.

507
00:36:20,105 --> 00:36:22,918
Why date her if it was going
to end like this?

508
00:36:23,670 --> 00:36:26,237
Why date her if you couldn't
take responsibility?

509
00:36:27,123 --> 00:36:30,439
Why date her if you couldn't protect her?

510
00:36:34,684 --> 00:36:37,370
Maybe it's because I'm raising a daughter,

511
00:36:37,791 --> 00:36:40,244
but that girl keeps weighing on me.

512
00:36:40,878 --> 00:36:42,651
Treated like a gold digger...

513
00:36:43,839 --> 00:36:45,762
by your family,

514
00:36:47,724 --> 00:36:50,291
bearing all that hurt and humiliation...

515
00:36:52,317 --> 00:36:54,601
how did she ever walk away from you?

516
00:37:13,472 --> 00:37:15,331
Delicious.

517
00:37:17,218 --> 00:37:20,857
Something this good,
and that nasty woman...

518
00:37:22,223 --> 00:37:23,736
Who was that woman?

519
00:37:24,331 --> 00:37:26,164
Are you asking me?

520
00:37:26,680 --> 00:37:28,577
Who else would I be asking?

521
00:37:28,602 --> 00:37:31,889
Was I asking the radish greens?
The radish kimchi?

522
00:37:33,924 --> 00:37:36,434
Who? Who do you mean?

523
00:37:36,949 --> 00:37:38,430
You know the one.

524
00:37:38,482 --> 00:37:41,433
She came in for side dishes in sunglasses,

525
00:37:41,458 --> 00:37:44,584
dressed like a spy. That awful woman.

526
00:37:45,371 --> 00:37:47,846
She asked if you were Han Gyu Rim.

527
00:37:47,935 --> 00:37:49,178
Who is she?

528
00:37:49,203 --> 00:37:51,196
- She asked my name?
- Yes.

529
00:37:52,358 --> 00:37:54,038
I have no idea.

530
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:55,536
No idea about what?

531
00:37:57,011 --> 00:37:59,677
Now that I think about it,
you put her up to it.

532
00:37:59,844 --> 00:38:02,619
To drive me out of my mind,

533
00:38:02,644 --> 00:38:05,504
you sent her to get revenge
for you, didn't you?

534
00:38:05,938 --> 00:38:07,893
I never did that.

535
00:38:07,918 --> 00:38:11,954
That's it. You two look alike, all right.

536
00:38:12,213 --> 00:38:14,008
You two definitely know each other.

537
00:38:14,340 --> 00:38:15,703
She must be a relative of yours.

538
00:38:15,864 --> 00:38:17,933
I don't have any relatives, Su Nam.

539
00:38:17,958 --> 00:38:21,595
Denying it won't help. One look and...

540
00:38:21,620 --> 00:38:23,123
(Gyeol's Teacher)

541
00:38:25,284 --> 00:38:27,838
Gyeol's teacher is calling.
Let me take this.

542
00:38:27,863 --> 00:38:29,737
That must be the nasty woman.

543
00:38:29,762 --> 00:38:32,869
Tell her to show her face
here one more time.

544
00:38:33,062 --> 00:38:36,905
I'll roll her up in green onion kimchi
and stuff her in a salted-fish jar.

545
00:38:37,525 --> 00:38:38,538
Hello, ma'am.

546
00:38:38,617 --> 00:38:41,549
Hello, this is Gyeol's homeroom teacher.

547
00:38:41,837 --> 00:38:44,315
Has Gyeol come home?

548
00:38:44,630 --> 00:38:47,383
I'm at the shop right now.

549
00:38:47,645 --> 00:38:49,451
Is something wrong with Gyeol?

550
00:38:52,770 --> 00:38:57,556
I'm not sure how to put this...

551
00:38:57,758 --> 00:39:00,570
Please just say it plainly.

552
00:39:01,715 --> 00:39:07,403
Did Gyeol cause some kind
of trouble at school?

553
00:39:07,550 --> 00:39:09,443
No, it's nothing like that...

554
00:39:13,204 --> 00:39:16,263
The children were watching
a science video,

555
00:39:17,710 --> 00:39:20,530
and blood types came up.

556
00:39:21,091 --> 00:39:22,857
Gyeol says...

557
00:39:23,958 --> 00:39:26,878
your blood type is O,

558
00:39:29,072 --> 00:39:33,392
and his is AB...

559
00:39:35,026 --> 00:39:36,317
Is that right?

560
00:39:37,645 --> 00:39:40,867
Yes, that's right. Why?

561
00:39:44,237 --> 00:39:46,686
A mother with type O blood...

562
00:39:47,408 --> 00:39:50,764
can't have a child with type AB.

563
00:39:52,185 --> 00:39:54,538
Regardless of the father's blood type.

564
00:39:58,124 --> 00:40:01,040
I know it's rude of me to bring this up,

565
00:40:01,554 --> 00:40:04,174
but to take better care of Gyeol,

566
00:40:04,199 --> 00:40:08,455
it really helps if I have
the right information about him.

567
00:40:09,651 --> 00:40:13,650
Could you be honest with me, just me?

568
00:40:15,511 --> 00:40:16,511
Gyeol is...

569
00:40:18,731 --> 00:40:20,271
my son.

570
00:40:20,644 --> 00:40:22,615
Of course. I know that.

571
00:40:22,717 --> 00:40:26,481
Just from his notebooks, I can see
how much you love him.

572
00:40:27,315 --> 00:40:28,971
Of all the parents in my class,

573
00:40:28,972 --> 00:40:32,803
I know better than anyone
that you're number one, by far.

574
00:40:34,283 --> 00:40:37,510
Did the children tease him a lot?

575
00:40:41,457 --> 00:40:42,892
I'm so sorry.

576
00:40:44,227 --> 00:40:46,458
It was recess, and I didn't catch it...

577
00:40:48,724 --> 00:40:50,124
I'm truly sorry.

578
00:40:55,526 --> 00:40:56,811
It's all right.

579
00:40:59,258 --> 00:41:03,748
It's my fault.

580
00:41:11,895 --> 00:41:15,481
(Son)

581
00:41:26,857 --> 00:41:28,444
Gyeol isn't picking up?

582
00:41:31,487 --> 00:41:36,517
What if he's really shaken?

583
00:41:38,351 --> 00:41:40,671
It must have hit him so hard.

584
00:41:44,424 --> 00:41:48,295
What do I do? My baby.

585
00:42:14,777 --> 00:42:16,777
Fine. Don't open it.

586
00:42:17,404 --> 00:42:19,850
What could you possibly say today?

587
00:42:23,530 --> 00:42:27,439
You'll only bring trouble today,
so stay away from the restaurant.

588
00:42:27,687 --> 00:42:30,024
Go home. Take the day.
Don't come tomorrow either.

589
00:42:35,398 --> 00:42:38,696
Seo Hyeon asked you not to call
until she sorts herself out.

590
00:43:04,850 --> 00:43:05,978
Gyeol.

591
00:43:08,997 --> 00:43:11,697
What's wrong with your face?
Were you crying?

592
00:43:17,077 --> 00:43:18,397
What is it?

593
00:43:21,425 --> 00:43:22,763
What happened?

594
00:43:44,144 --> 00:43:45,204
All done?

595
00:43:45,911 --> 00:43:48,444
It's okay. I can do it myself.

596
00:43:55,198 --> 00:43:56,471
Want some warm milk?

597
00:43:56,496 --> 00:44:00,001
No, cold milk. With a ton of ice.

598
00:44:13,438 --> 00:44:14,818
Drink the warm milk.

599
00:44:14,904 --> 00:44:17,457
Cold milk on an upset stomach
gives you diarrhea.

600
00:44:17,510 --> 00:44:18,517
Okay.

601
00:44:21,658 --> 00:44:23,558
Want me to order you anything else?

602
00:44:27,344 --> 00:44:31,504
I already said my goodbye, and I'm sorry
for showing up again.

603
00:44:32,797 --> 00:44:34,222
Don't be sorry.

604
00:44:34,970 --> 00:44:38,578
It's fine. I missed you too.

605
00:44:39,618 --> 00:44:43,997
Of everyone I know, you're the smartest.

606
00:44:44,757 --> 00:44:47,450
Gyu Yeong is smart too,

607
00:44:47,685 --> 00:44:52,399
but she's such a pain that I can't
go to her for advice.

608
00:44:53,190 --> 00:44:55,083
Right. Good call.

609
00:44:56,204 --> 00:44:58,551
Can I ask what's on your mind?

610
00:45:13,631 --> 00:45:14,724
What is this?

611
00:45:15,464 --> 00:45:17,850
A blood type inheritance chart.

612
00:45:18,377 --> 00:45:20,996
I know that much, but why?

613
00:45:21,245 --> 00:45:24,404
My mom is type O, but I'm type AB.

614
00:45:27,810 --> 00:45:31,410
See? You already know.

615
00:45:31,770 --> 00:45:35,316
You always spot what's wrong right away.

616
00:45:38,165 --> 00:45:40,078
Are you sure you have it right?

617
00:45:41,624 --> 00:45:43,669
Your mom's blood type is O, fine,

618
00:45:45,021 --> 00:45:47,051
but are you certain yours is AB?

619
00:45:47,203 --> 00:45:48,870
I'm certain.

620
00:45:51,643 --> 00:45:54,983
A lot of people have their own blood type
wrong these days.

621
00:45:55,464 --> 00:45:57,764
Let's go to a clinic nearby
and check it again together.

622
00:45:57,789 --> 00:46:02,258
If it's still AB after we check,

623
00:46:02,346 --> 00:46:05,763
then I'm not my mom's son, am I?

624
00:46:09,984 --> 00:46:12,260
Let's talk to your mom first.

625
00:46:12,285 --> 00:46:16,118
No. I don't want to see her.

626
00:46:28,877 --> 00:46:31,885
- What is it?
- I'm going to wash my face.

627
00:46:41,671 --> 00:46:46,218
(Mom)

628
00:46:53,005 --> 00:46:54,858
Gyeol, where are you?

629
00:46:55,037 --> 00:46:57,630
Why aren't you answering me?

630
00:46:58,884 --> 00:47:00,497
This is Kim Mu Jin.

631
00:47:01,563 --> 00:47:04,310
Why are you answering Gyeol's phone?

632
00:47:04,824 --> 00:47:06,964
He's with me right now.

633
00:47:07,890 --> 00:47:09,610
He came to find me.

634
00:47:11,731 --> 00:47:13,032
Where are you?

635
00:47:13,332 --> 00:47:15,224
I'll come to you right now.

636
00:47:18,244 --> 00:47:21,289
Not right now, I think. A little later.

637
00:47:24,898 --> 00:47:27,783
Gyeol seems pretty shaken,

638
00:47:29,231 --> 00:47:31,791
and I don't think he wants to see you.

639
00:47:35,064 --> 00:47:37,317
Try not to worry too much and wait.

640
00:47:37,342 --> 00:47:40,275
I'll calm him down and bring him home.

641
00:48:04,991 --> 00:48:07,318
(Ji Yeol's Wife)

642
00:48:13,937 --> 00:48:17,250
We just got back from the hospital.

643
00:48:17,935 --> 00:48:23,334
The doctor says he'll probably
need another surgery.

644
00:48:25,098 --> 00:48:27,751
Ji Yeol doesn't know I'm calling.

645
00:48:27,995 --> 00:48:30,312
He told me never to call you.

646
00:48:31,823 --> 00:48:36,901
We have nowhere else to turn,
and I was desperate.

647
00:48:37,818 --> 00:48:41,890
It's all right. You did the right thing.

648
00:48:42,577 --> 00:48:46,185
Send me the bill when it comes.

649
00:48:46,766 --> 00:48:47,963
I'm sorry.

650
00:48:48,506 --> 00:48:51,527
You must be struggling too,
and all I do is ask for money.

651
00:48:53,725 --> 00:48:57,506
But this is all because of you.

652
00:48:58,271 --> 00:49:01,917
I hope you don't think too badly of us.

653
00:49:40,064 --> 00:49:42,757
- What is this?
- Keys to a car driven once.

654
00:49:42,837 --> 00:49:44,157
Just take it.

655
00:49:47,137 --> 00:49:50,160
Do you know
how hard it was to track you down?

656
00:49:50,391 --> 00:49:52,557
I waited in that parking lot for an hour.

657
00:49:53,524 --> 00:49:55,454
Quit playing around and get lost.

658
00:49:59,245 --> 00:50:01,576
I have a third car besides that one.

659
00:50:01,778 --> 00:50:03,571
Just think of it as a gift.

660
00:50:05,426 --> 00:50:08,840
Yun Gi said you'd do anything for money.

661
00:50:09,772 --> 00:50:11,157
Was he wrong?

662
00:50:14,117 --> 00:50:17,286
Yun Gi said you'd sell your soul
for the right price.

663
00:50:17,317 --> 00:50:19,210
Was he lying to me?

664
00:50:29,870 --> 00:50:32,184
Is this about Hui Na and Su Chan?

665
00:50:32,209 --> 00:50:34,777
Friendship, love,
what does any of it matter?

666
00:50:35,158 --> 00:50:36,966
In the end it's all money.

667
00:50:36,991 --> 00:50:40,258
People betray
and con each other over money.

668
00:50:49,445 --> 00:50:51,139
You've got that much money?

669
00:50:52,191 --> 00:50:54,045
Yes. I have money.

670
00:50:54,391 --> 00:50:56,600
Not just a lot. An obscene amount.

671
00:50:56,678 --> 00:50:58,533
My family is filthy rich.

672
00:51:02,845 --> 00:51:04,069
You want to sleep with me?

673
00:51:06,483 --> 00:51:09,179
- What?
- Then pay me. I'll do it.

674
00:51:09,745 --> 00:51:11,545
But I'm expensive.

675
00:51:12,843 --> 00:51:15,532
- Listen, Han Gyu O.
- No cars, no cards.

676
00:51:15,557 --> 00:51:18,137
If you're serious, bring cash.
An obscene amount.

677
00:51:18,418 --> 00:51:21,984
Enough to make me want to sell my soul.

678
00:51:58,363 --> 00:51:59,377
Kwon Hui Na.

679
00:52:00,100 --> 00:52:03,085
It's Han Gyu O. Meet me once.

680
00:52:04,110 --> 00:52:05,134
Just once.

681
00:52:19,231 --> 00:52:20,500
I'm not asking for more.

682
00:52:20,705 --> 00:52:22,527
Give me one hour.

683
00:52:25,604 --> 00:52:27,305
(That gigolo)

684
00:52:28,552 --> 00:52:30,353
(Contact Blocked)

685
00:52:36,216 --> 00:52:39,999
(Kwon Hui Na)

686
00:52:51,500 --> 00:52:52,765
(Suragan Side Dishes)

687
00:52:52,790 --> 00:52:57,043
Gyeol says your blood type is O,

688
00:52:57,342 --> 00:53:01,183
and his is AB.

689
00:53:02,375 --> 00:53:08,569
A mother with type O blood
can't have a child with type AB.

690
00:53:12,302 --> 00:53:14,882
Gyeol seems pretty shaken,

691
00:53:16,054 --> 00:53:18,562
and he doesn't want to see you right now.

692
00:53:39,977 --> 00:53:42,459
How is this one selling?

693
00:53:43,037 --> 00:53:47,184
It sells well. The ladies
play a lot of golf these days.

694
00:53:49,182 --> 00:53:52,208
Did you design this one, Director?

695
00:53:58,533 --> 00:54:01,651
- The color came out great, didn't it?
- It really did.

696
00:54:04,391 --> 00:54:07,659
Is she crying?

697
00:54:31,643 --> 00:54:37,866
(Chairman Jang Hun Tae)

698
00:54:50,213 --> 00:54:51,727
That jerk.

699
00:55:27,944 --> 00:55:29,209
What's with the lips?

700
00:55:31,518 --> 00:55:35,369
I wore this lipstick because you like it.
Too sexy?

701
00:55:37,697 --> 00:55:40,084
Sure. Insanely sexy.

702
00:55:41,438 --> 00:55:46,275
By the way, can we just register
the marriage this week?

703
00:55:46,711 --> 00:55:48,982
What's the rush?
We can do it after the wedding.

704
00:55:49,203 --> 00:55:53,193
I want it in writing, fast,
that you belong to me.

705
00:55:53,510 --> 00:55:57,464
Since when does Han Gyu Yeong
live and die by a piece of paper?

706
00:55:57,505 --> 00:56:00,889
I do. I love paperwork. Anything official.

707
00:56:01,684 --> 00:56:03,594
I'm starving. Where's the food?

708
00:56:04,418 --> 00:56:05,431
Heung Sik is coming.

709
00:56:05,524 --> 00:56:08,457
Who? Cho Heung Sik?

710
00:56:09,071 --> 00:56:10,111
What for?

711
00:56:10,525 --> 00:56:13,825
He called while you were in the restroom,
so I told him to come.

712
00:56:13,977 --> 00:56:15,297
He happened to be nearby.

713
00:56:15,644 --> 00:56:17,487
Without even asking me?

714
00:56:17,532 --> 00:56:20,191
Why crash someone's date
without reading the room?

715
00:56:22,164 --> 00:56:24,768
- Seong Uk.
- Hey.

716
00:56:28,678 --> 00:56:30,594
Been a while, Gyu Yeong.

717
00:56:30,724 --> 00:56:34,663
- Yes. How have you been?
- Good.

718
00:56:35,574 --> 00:56:39,404
I hope I'm not intruding
on the two of you.

719
00:56:39,443 --> 00:56:42,445
We're not on a date.
We were just hungry, so we came to eat.

720
00:56:43,291 --> 00:56:45,622
- Have you eaten?
- No.

721
00:56:46,861 --> 00:56:49,391
There he is. My lunch.

722
00:56:52,529 --> 00:56:53,603
What?

723
00:56:55,110 --> 00:56:57,316
- I'm your lunch?
- That's right.

724
00:56:57,498 --> 00:56:59,376
I'm eating you for lunch today.

725
00:57:00,022 --> 00:57:01,564
Let's sit down first.

726
00:57:01,648 --> 00:57:03,819
Sure, but hold on.

727
00:57:04,492 --> 00:57:06,287
Why am I your lunch?

728
00:57:06,935 --> 00:57:08,698
Take a guess.

729
00:57:09,663 --> 00:57:11,223
What is it?

730
00:57:12,518 --> 00:57:14,155
What kind of lunch?

731
00:57:17,828 --> 00:57:19,316
A free lunch?

732
00:57:25,200 --> 00:57:26,852
You've got something on your glass.

733
00:57:30,395 --> 00:57:33,162
- Hey.
- Honey, I'm so sorry.

734
00:57:33,187 --> 00:57:36,556
Hey, you really are something.

735
00:57:48,577 --> 00:57:52,838
Be careful. It was obvious
you spilled that wine on purpose.

736
00:57:53,484 --> 00:57:55,224
And change up your routine.

737
00:57:55,249 --> 00:57:56,861
Didn't you spill wine last time too?

738
00:57:56,944 --> 00:57:58,227
I told you I'd kill you.

739
00:57:58,429 --> 00:58:00,415
I said I'd kill you
if you ruined my wedding.

740
00:58:00,440 --> 00:58:01,445
Then kill me.

741
00:58:02,291 --> 00:58:06,828
If I didn't know, fine.
But I do, and I can't look away.

742
00:58:07,943 --> 00:58:09,516
If Gyu Rim finds out,

743
00:58:09,541 --> 00:58:12,415
she'll break your legs
to stop this wedding.

744
00:58:12,976 --> 00:58:14,797
That Han Gyu Rim, honestly.

745
00:58:15,262 --> 00:58:17,711
The day I marry, she and I
are complete strangers.

746
00:58:17,810 --> 00:58:21,834
Whether I wash dishes with a robot vacuum
or fry eggs in omega-3,

747
00:58:22,110 --> 00:58:25,558
she can't touch my life,
and she's agreed not to.

748
00:58:26,816 --> 00:58:28,412
Ever heard of cutting ties?

749
00:58:30,524 --> 00:58:32,864
You're hopeless.

750
00:58:33,158 --> 00:58:35,734
You act so clever,

751
00:58:35,944 --> 00:58:39,376
so why walk into a marriage
you know will be miserable?

752
00:58:39,497 --> 00:58:42,908
What makes me miserable isn't love.
It's money.

753
00:58:43,083 --> 00:58:44,303
Understood?

754
00:58:46,658 --> 00:58:49,826
How much do you need?

755
00:58:49,851 --> 00:58:51,519
I'll lend it to you interest-free.

756
00:58:51,787 --> 00:58:53,120
Give me a break.

757
00:58:54,340 --> 00:58:55,926
Get lost before Seong Uk comes back.

758
00:58:55,951 --> 00:58:58,577
Unless you plan to live my life for me,
get lost.

759
00:59:03,249 --> 00:59:06,622
Once you draw the knife,
you've got to cut something.

760
00:59:07,838 --> 00:59:12,117
Give me a forehead flick and we're even.

761
00:59:12,318 --> 00:59:13,519
Heung Sik.

762
00:59:21,198 --> 00:59:24,263
Where did that punk disappear to?

763
00:59:36,252 --> 00:59:38,493
That crazy son of a...

764
00:59:38,518 --> 00:59:40,728
Hey, you punk.

765
00:59:50,448 --> 00:59:51,957
My tooth.

766
00:59:52,791 --> 00:59:54,983
My tooth came out!

767
00:59:57,739 --> 00:59:59,358
My tooth.

768
01:00:00,135 --> 01:00:02,661
My tooth is gone.

769
01:00:02,793 --> 01:00:04,441
Are you even human?

770
01:00:04,584 --> 01:00:06,976
This is an animal, not a person.

771
01:00:08,165 --> 01:00:10,551
I'm dying.

772
01:00:10,576 --> 01:00:11,794
Honey.

773
01:00:11,871 --> 01:00:15,909
Honey, help me.

774
01:00:22,703 --> 01:00:24,005
My tooth.

775
01:00:24,371 --> 01:00:25,944
Where did my tooth go?

776
01:00:25,969 --> 01:00:29,951
My tooth.

777
01:00:30,464 --> 01:00:32,175
Cho Heung Sik.

778
01:01:01,531 --> 01:01:05,617
So, are you feeling any better?

779
01:01:11,018 --> 01:01:12,245
Is there anything you want to eat?

780
01:01:17,251 --> 01:01:19,925
Then who is my mom?

781
01:01:20,184 --> 01:01:23,046
And who is my dad?

782
01:01:26,832 --> 01:01:31,853
Did my mom find me under a bridge too?

783
01:01:34,350 --> 01:01:37,748
Where's the bridge she found me under?

784
01:01:39,711 --> 01:01:41,305
Gyeol.

785
01:01:41,877 --> 01:01:46,839
If you know that bridge, take me there.

786
01:02:04,203 --> 01:02:05,690
Drink some water.

787
01:02:06,157 --> 01:02:08,241
Keep crying
like that and you'll dehydrate.

788
01:02:55,137 --> 01:02:57,118
I hear you're with Gyeol.

789
01:02:57,601 --> 01:02:59,958
Gyu Rim wants you to call her phone.

790
01:03:00,325 --> 01:03:04,791
I'll hear what went wrong in person.
Sending you her number too.

791
01:03:16,530 --> 01:03:19,204
- Hello?
- This is Kim Mu Jin.

792
01:03:19,984 --> 01:03:22,091
Is Gyeol with you right now?

793
01:03:22,632 --> 01:03:23,665
I'm sorry.

794
01:03:24,378 --> 01:03:27,368
I knew you'd be worried,
and I still didn't call.

795
01:03:27,784 --> 01:03:30,456
Where are you? I'll come to you right now.

796
01:03:32,077 --> 01:03:36,373
Gyeol says he doesn't want
to go home today,

797
01:03:37,792 --> 01:03:39,668
that he wants to stay with me.

798
01:03:41,758 --> 01:03:44,795
No. Why would he stay with you
when he has a home?

799
01:03:45,157 --> 01:03:47,688
I'll come to you. Where are you?

800
01:03:57,316 --> 01:03:59,704
- Please wait a moment, sir.
- Sure.

801
01:04:09,697 --> 01:04:11,473
Let me take him. I'll carry him.

802
01:04:11,904 --> 01:04:12,998
I'll take him for you.

803
01:04:13,205 --> 01:04:14,746
I have a taxi waiting.

804
01:04:15,944 --> 01:04:18,663
To the taxi, then. Let me carry him.

805
01:04:43,791 --> 01:04:45,458
What kind of life have you had?

806
01:04:54,131 --> 01:04:55,614
What kind of life have you been living,

807
01:04:57,591 --> 01:04:59,331
these past eight years since you left me?

808
01:05:31,317 --> 01:05:33,445
(Love on the Menu)

809
01:05:33,492 --> 01:05:36,183
- Ma'am.
- Since when am I your ma'am?

810
01:05:36,208 --> 01:05:38,660
Since you're not my mother, ma'am.

811
01:05:38,685 --> 01:05:40,626
Why did you leave me behind?

812
01:05:40,651 --> 01:05:42,956
What's the deal with Gyeol?
He's really not Gyu Rim's son?

813
01:05:42,981 --> 01:05:45,021
I thought she gave birth to him.

814
01:05:45,171 --> 01:05:47,898
She even showed me a photo
of the baby in her belly.

815
01:05:47,923 --> 01:05:49,529
She showed you an ultrasound?

816
01:05:49,584 --> 01:05:50,786
Where are you right now?

817
01:05:50,811 --> 01:05:52,156
I never expected to meet you like this.

818
01:05:52,351 --> 01:05:54,427
Don't you know me? Han Gyu O.

819
01:05:54,565 --> 01:05:56,088
Divorce Mom first.

820
01:05:56,139 --> 01:05:57,273
How dare you.

821
01:05:57,373 --> 01:05:58,534
You don't know your place.

822
01:05:58,593 --> 01:06:00,493
That girl is my eldest daughter.

823
01:06:01,384 --> 01:06:02,964
Where are you, Gyu Rim?

824
01:06:04,003 --> 01:06:05,903
Dramaday.me
